<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    No App Sandbox. This is a Developer ID app that spawns ssh/mosh/devmachine
    on the PATH and reads arbitrary files the owner points it at (Files
    window, workspace folders); the sandbox would need broad exceptions for
    both and buys nothing a non-sandboxed, notarized, hardened-runtime app
    does not already have.

    Hardened Runtime turns on a set of restrictions by default (no unsigned
    executable memory, no DYLD_* injection, no debugger attach, library
    validation) and every one of them is fine as-is:
      - zmx ships as its own embedded, separately-signed executable and runs
        as a child process (Process/NSTask), never dlopen'd into this process,
        so library validation does not touch it and
        `com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation` is not needed.
      - mosh-client is the same: its own signed executable in
        Contents/Helpers, run as a child process, with protobuf linked in
        statically and only system libraries left dynamic.
      - SwiftTerm, HighlightSwift and swift-markdown-ui link in as ordinary
        signed frameworks/dylibs from the same signing identity — hardened
        runtime's default library validation already allows same-team code.
      - No JIT, no unsigned/writable executable memory, no AppleScript/Apple
        Events, no location, no downloaded-executable exec.

    Camera and microphone are the two keys below. The preview's web view asks
    for them on a page's behalf (a video call in the app being built), the
    person answers per site, and macOS then asks once for the app. Without
    these keys Hardened Runtime refuses the device even after both said yes.

    If a future dependency needs one of the `com.apple.security.cs.*`
    relaxations, add it here with the same kind of comment: which binary
    needs it and why.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key><true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
